1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Germany scored 4 goals in 6 minutes…

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,900
against Brazil. In Brazil.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,600
July 8, 2014.

4
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:12,000
A World Cup semi-final in Belo Horizonte.

5
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:15,000
Brazil were without Neymar, injured.

6
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:18,700
And their captain, Thiago Silva, was suspended.

7
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:23,100
11 minutes. Thomas Müller, unmarked from a corner.

8
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:25,400
1–0.

9
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,700
23 minutes. Miroslav Klose.

10
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:34,300
His 16th World Cup goal… a new record, passing Brazil’s Ronaldo.

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,900
Then Toni Kroos scores. And again.

12
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:42,200
Then Sami Khedira. 5–0… after 29 minutes.

13
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,400
André Schürrle added 2 more.

14
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,600
Oscar got one back at the end. 7–1.

15
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:50,500
5 days later, Germany won the World Cup.

16
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:54,800
Worst scoreline you’ve ever seen? Tell me in the comments.
